# Privacy Policy

ChromaPress is an open-source desktop application for building, customizing and verifying Linux installation images.

## Data collection

ChromaPress does not intentionally collect, store, transmit or sell personal user data.

ChromaPress does not include advertising, user tracking, analytics or telemetry operated by the ChromaPress project.

Project files, configuration files and ISO images processed by ChromaPress remain on the user's own computer unless the user explicitly chooses to transfer or publish them elsewhere.

## External services

Some user-initiated operations may interact with external services, such as Linux package repositories, software repositories or other resources selected by the user.

Those services may have their own privacy policies and are outside the control of the ChromaPress project.

## Diagnostic information

ChromaPress may display local diagnostic, build and verification information required for its operation. This information is not automatically sent to the ChromaPress developer.

If a user voluntarily submits an issue, log or diagnostic information through GitHub or another communication channel, that information is provided voluntarily by the user.

## Open source

The ChromaPress source code is publicly available for inspection:

https://github.com/Janus5G/ChromaPress

## Contact

Privacy or security questions concerning ChromaPress may be submitted through the project's GitHub repository.

